Mac run of `ROUNDUP_ALLOW_WINDOW=1 just perf-keystroke --out target/perf-keystroke-before.json` on PR #3755 (branch `build/issue-3550-mac`, `853f9440b`, rebased on `59cff55ca`). **Exit 0**: every run had p95 10 ms and 0 dropped keys.

Cause: the Workstream's Agent Terminal showed about 200 ms after the shell bubble printed `ready` and took focus. That folded the bubble (display none), and xterm's IntersectionObserver paused rendering, so the echoes were parsed but never rendered. Details are in #3755.

MacBook Pro M4 Max, 16 CPUs, macOS 26.0.1, AC power, Low Power Mode off; loads 5.8 / 4.4 / 3.1.

